#!/bin/sh
# Standalone Ports Script Template
#
# PocketTracker's entry in Onion's ports list. Onion executes this file and it hands the work to
# Onion's own standalone launcher, which resolves Games/PocketTracker/ and runs launch.sh inside it.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ THE WHOLE REASON THIS IS A PORT AND NOT AN APP-SHELF ENTRY: Onion records play time, launch
# count and the Game Switcher's recent list only for what `check_is_game` in .tmp_update/runtime.sh
# accepts, and that test is "the launch command names /mnt/SDCARD/Roms/". Anything started from
# /mnt/SDCARD/App/ is recorded nowhere. It is the install path that decides, not a setting.
#
# ⚠️ THE FILE NAME IS THE NAME THE TRACKER STORES, and `.port` is the extension Onion's ports system
# lists (Emu/PORTS/config.json carries `"extlist": "port|miyoocmd"`). Onion's import script renames
# this file to `.notfound` when it cannot find the payload named below, and back again when it can —
# so a package that really carries its files stays visible without the user importing anything.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ THE AUDIO HANDOVER FLAG BELOW STAYS 0 EVEN THOUGH THE SOUND SERVICE MUST BE STOPPED. Onion's
# launcher stops it and continues in the same breath; the hardware releases the audio device a
# fraction of a second later, and starting into that gap is exactly the "app closes straight back to
# the menu" failure this port already had once. launch.sh stops it AND waits for the release — and
# it can only do that if it is the one that stopped it, since its wait is skipped when it finds
# nothing running to stop.
#
# ⚠️ The performance-governor flag stays 0 as well. Nothing has measured what it does to this app on
# this hardware, and a packaging change is the wrong place to ship an unmeasured one.
#
# ⚠️ Every `Name=` line here is READ BY Onion's import script with a plain grep, first match wins.
# A commented-out or example assignment anywhere in this file is picked up as the real one.

# main configuration :
GameName="PocketTracker"
GameDir="PocketTracker"
GameExecutable="launch.sh"
GameDataFile="pockettracker"

# additional configuration
KillAudioserver=0
PerformanceMode=0

# specific to this port :
Arguments=""

# running command line :
/mnt/SDCARD/Emu/PORTS/launch_standalone.sh "$GameName" "$GameDir" "$GameExecutable" "$Arguments" "$GameDataFile" "$KillAudioserver" "$PerformanceMode"
